Here is an example of a C# method that can be used to download a MongoDB document:
```
using MongoDB.Driver;
using System.IO;

public void DownloadDocument(string url, string collectionName, out string contentType, out byte[] content)
{
    var client = new MongoClient("mongodb://localhost:27017");
    var database = client.GetDatabase("mydatabase");
    var collection = database.GetCollection<BsonDocument>(collectionName);
    var filter = Builders<BsonDocument>.Filter.Empty;
    var document = collection.Find(filter).FirstOrDefault();

    if (document!= null)
    {
        contentType = "application/" + document.ContentType;
        content = document.Content;
    }
    else
    {
        contentType = null;
        content = null;
    }
}
```
This method takes three parameters:

* `url` is the URL of the MongoDB database.
* `collectionName` is the name of the collection in the database.
* `out contentType, out content` are output parameters that will be set to the content type and content of the downloaded document, respectively.

The method first connects to the MongoDB database using the `MongoClient` class and gets the specified collection using the `GetCollection` method. It then uses the `Find` method to retrieve the first document from the collection, and sets the `contentType` and `content` output parameters to the appropriate values if a document is found. If no document is found, the `contentType` and `content` output parameters are set to `null`.

Note that this method uses the MongoDB C# driver, which allows you to interact with MongoDB from C#. To use the driver, you will need to add a reference to the MongoDB driver package in your project and make sure that your project is targeting a.NET framework that is compatible with the driver.
